      {
        "id": "530777",
        "date_added": "2026-11-21 13:21:23",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static analysis only. Rust ELF, not packed. It calls itself easyshell-http-beacon-implant. Server in clear text in a config template slot: https://192.3.31[.]148:8443 (same as the ThreatFox IOC). Unused slots start with markers !ES/\u003cn\u003e/\u003cTAG\u003e/. Threads es-beacon-uplink, es-mux-agg, es-idle-reaper; process shown as [kworker/0:0] (Triage run). RANSOMWARE and ELF_Packer_Dropper_Fileless_Armhf are false positives (the word \"encrypted\"; ChaCha20 constant from the crypto libs). Write-up, YARA rule, IOCs: https://github.com/cyberpascal1101/linux-malware-research/tree/main/easyshell-rust-implant"
      }
    ],
